{"cluster_id": "C-3470", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B041-077"], "canonical_claim": "The chosen key layout uses cas/ref_catalog, cas/refs/<ns>/_head, cas/refs/<ns>/<incarnation>/_node/<sequence16>-<sha256-of-canonical-node>.zst, cas/refs/<ns>/<incarnation>/_snapshot/<covered-sequence16>-<sha256-of-canonical-snapshot>.zst, cas/manifests/<ns>/<incarnation>/<build-id>/..., and roots/<ns>/<incarnation>/....", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_simplify_design.md#L48-L67"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3471", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B041-120", "B041-121", "B041-122"], "canonical_claim": "The public ClickHouse tree has no table-level durable part-registry interface such as IPartRegistry, IDataPartsStorage, or IPartCatalog.; CAS table refs represent the filesystem-like physical inventory, not the richer MergeTreeData active-parts registry or Keeper's expected per-replica part set.; DataPartStorageContentAddressed addresses only part identity -> manifest entries and files; it does not replace table identity -> durable set of physical parts.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/datapartstorage-content-addressed-design-concern.md#L193-L210", "docs/superpowers/cas/datapartstorage-content-addressed-design-concern.md#L224-L232", "docs/superpowers/cas/datapartstorage-content-addressed-design-concern.md#L234-L244"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3472", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B042-003"], "canonical_claim": "For `Layout::parseNamespaceFileKey`, a key carrying `/_files/` is only a necessary trigger for namespace-file parsing, not sufficient proof that it is a real namespace file, because `Layout::mountpointObjectKey` does not enforce the `_files` reservation.", "issue_ids": ["D1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/deferred-docs-fixes.md#d1-parse-namespace-file-key-contract"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3473", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B043-065"], "canonical_claim": "Raw object-storage paths are not a meaningful CAS filesystem interface: logical navigation from a part/ref to tree entries and blob content requires decoding manifests and trees; introspection must provide decoded views.", "issue_ids": ["B169"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/random_notes.md#lines-215-224"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3474", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B045-057"], "canonical_claim": "The fixture identity derivation is byte-for-byte equivalent to `NamespaceLifeId::stageATransition`: it uses `sipHash128` over the namespace string bytes, maps a zero hash to `1`, and calls `NamespaceLifeId::fromCatalogEntry(ns, incarnation)`; existing fixture keys therefore remain unchanged.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1c3-report.md#L54-L63"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3475", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B046-029"], "canonical_claim": "The shared isCleanRelativeNamespaceFileName predicate is used by both Layout::namespaceFileKey and Layout::parseNamespaceFileKey, eliminating the prior parser asymmetry in which the parser accepted nonempty dirty names that the writer rejected.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t3-report.md#L168-L174", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t3-review.md#L164-L176"]}
