{"cluster_id": "C-3484", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-088"], "canonical_claim": "CAS discovery LISTs use fixed prefixes: `cas/ns/stream/`, `cas/ns/`, `cas/manifests/`, `blobs/` (deliberately without the algorithm segment so one recursive LIST covers every hash algorithm), `roots/`, and `gc/server-roots/`. The `staging/` prefix is a top-level sibling that no GC LIST ever touches \u2014 it is reclaimed only by its own server's next mount.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#key-table"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3485", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-288"], "canonical_claim": "`listDirectory`/`existsDirectory` branch by path shape in a fixed, load-bearing order \u2014 shadow, atomic-shard-dir, table-uuid, part-file, table-subdir, generic mirrored LIST \u2014 because `store/<u3>` and non-Atomic `data/<db>` would otherwise collide, so `isAtomicShardDir` must be consulted before `parseTableUuid`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/01-frontend.md#e-directory-listing-exists"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3486", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-290"], "canonical_claim": "Every CAS key family is rooted at `POOL = pool_prefix`: blob body `POOL/blobs/<algo>/<S>/<hex>` (self-describing, `<S>`=first 2 hex chars); blob meta `POOL/blobs/<algo>/<S>/<hex>.meta`; part manifest `POOL/cas/manifests/<ns>/<epoch-hex>-<seq-hex>/<NNNNNN>.proto`; ref log txn `POOL/cas/refs/<ns>/_log/<render>`; ref snapshot `POOL/cas/refs/<ns>/_snap/<render>.proto`; ref cleanup marker `POOL/cas/refs/<ns>/_cleanup/<render>`; verbatim namespace file `POOL/roots/<ns>/_files/<name>`; plain mountpoint object `POOL/roots/<key>`; pool meta `POOL/_pool_meta`; GC state/heartbeat `POOL/gc/state`, `POOL/gc/hb`; GC generation artifacts `POOL/gc/gen/<gen>/attempt/<a>/...`; server-root control `POOL/gc/server-roots/<srid>/{owner,epoch,mount}`; opt-in staging `POOL/staging/<mount_id>/...` (a distinct top-level sibling GC never LISTs).", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#3-2-key-layout-layout-caslayout-h-blobkey-parseblobkey-in-casbuild-cpp-866-confirmed"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3487", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-294"], "canonical_claim": "`CasPoolMeta` (`_pool_meta`) is a pure protobuf `PoolMetaProto` holding `pool_id`, `root_shards`, `blob_header_len`, `min_reader_generation`, and a sorted append-only `algos_used[]`; invariants are `root_shards >= 1` and `blob_header_len` 8-aligned in `[96, 16384]`; admitting a new hash algorithm raises `min_reader_generation` to `G_BUILD` in the same CAS.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#3-4-on-storage-formats-with-versioning-confirmed"]}
